{"title":"2002 IMO Shortlist Problems/A2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Notes\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notes</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/e/eeedac0c276d2696238eac2fb824b2eb3b2d7412.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_b, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"11\" /> be an infinite sequence of real numbers, for which there exists a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbc9e92f88e53e090863da7488a48efd1413a3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le a_i \\le c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, such that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb7470fbce674a765fd036088a38d7b2949d5d70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_i - a_j | \\ge \\frac{1}{i+j} \\mbox{ for all }i,\\; j \\mbox{ with } i \\neq j.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"296\" height=\"40\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66fc9dbd593f92b7f0a52a17fc98b275c19671e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For some fixed value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa35d9fc104207e09a712110ac81612c5b279a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Permutation\" title=\"Permutation\">permutation</a> of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> natural numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfc3d47e658f06a41218822d21ecba217f8e30ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{\\sigma(1)} , \\ldots a_{\\sigma(n)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"13\" /> is an increasing sequence.  Then we have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af1dbd2d0007f971b8588cd7dbfd372ca897f5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix} a_{\\sigma(n)} - a_{\\sigma(1)} &amp;=\\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\left| a_{\\sigma(i+1)} - a_{\\sigma(i)} \\right| \\qquad \\quad \\\\ &amp;\\ge\\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\frac{1}{\\sigma(i+1) + \\sigma(i)} \\qquad (*) \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"327\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Now, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality\" title=\"Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality</a>, we have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/7929498ae46c63fef0db39be956655c4485f8cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix} \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\frac{1}{\\sigma(i+1) + \\sigma(i)} \\right) \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\sigma(i+1) + \\sigma(i) \\right) &amp; \\ge &amp; (n-1)^2 \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\\\ \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\frac{1}{\\sigma(i+1) + \\sigma(i)} &amp; \\ge &amp;\\frac{(n-1)^2}{2 \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} (\\sigma_{i}) - \\sigma(1) - \\sigma(n)} \\\\ &amp; \\ge &amp;\\frac{(n-1)^2}{n(n+1) -3} \\qquad \\qquad \\\\ &amp; \\ge &amp;\\frac{n-1}{n+3} . \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\quad \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -52px\" width=\"535\" height=\"113\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Thus for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we must have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165cb65f6ecb032c54b3b48fc2d5a532d853a698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\ge \\frac{n-1}{n+3} = 1 - \\frac{4}{n+3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"184\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> must be at least 1, Q.E.D.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We proceed to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d02e715e7f7195675151570530c5b62ba7b2744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> as in Solution 1.  We now note that by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=RMS-AM-GM-HM\" title=\"RMS-AM-GM-HM\"> AM-HM Inequality</a>,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efe7bbd4a2a7cb3e38efad702f27a243b6d41914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix} \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\frac{1}{\\sigma(i+1) + \\sigma(i)} &amp; \\ge &amp;\\frac{(n-1)^2}{\\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\left[ \\sigma(i+1) + \\sigma(i) \\right] } \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\\\ &amp; &gt; &amp;\\frac{(n-1)^2}{\\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\left[ \\sigma(i+1) + \\sigma(i) \\right] + \\sigma(n) + \\sigma(1) } \\\\ &amp; = &amp;\\frac{(n-1)^2}{n(n+1)} . \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\quad \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -39px\" width=\"385\" height=\"89\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Thus for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we have two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> that differ by more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9aeba54b38b3fae2a41c8820a68652b2e187297.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(n-1)^2}{n(n+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"69\" height=\"43\" />.  But this becomes arbitrarily close to 1 as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> becomes arbitrarily large.  Hence if we had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132e039bfc02ad143e738f1cc566c08009d31947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, then we could obtain a contradiction, so we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66fc9dbd593f92b7f0a52a17fc98b275c19671e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, Q.E.D.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Notes\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The chief difficulty of this problem seems to be obtaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d02e715e7f7195675151570530c5b62ba7b2744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />; once this result has been obtained, there are many ways to conclude.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2002 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2002 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=17331\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018045530\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 147/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 353/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5404/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.327      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.327      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4378:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018045530 and revision id 27491. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}